a\xa0non‐pharmacological pain management strategy to a no‐treatment control group (15\xa0different strategies).\xa0In   
addition, we also analysed studies when the unique effect of adding a non‐pharmacological pain management strategy onto 
another pain management strategy could be assessed (i.e. additive effects on\xa0a sweet solution, non‐nutritive sucking,
or swaddling) (three strategies). The eligible control groups for these additive studies were sweet solution only,      
