### 3. Additional context:                                                                                              
The screening followed strict adherence to the protocol which explicitly excludes kangaroo care, sucrose,               
breastfeeding/breast milk, and music. Studies using these interventions as primary comparisons were excluded even if    
they also tested other interventions. Additive effect studies (testing unique effects added to sweet solution, NNS, or  
swaddling) would be eligible only if the control was sweet solution/NNS/swaddling alone - but most such studies in this 
chunk used sucrose as part of the intervention itself, leading to exclusion.                                            
                                                                                                                        
The included studies represent diverse non-pharmacological strategies: tactile (massage, facilitated tucking,           
swaddling), auditory (maternal voice, white noise), olfactory (amniotic fluid, familiar scents), visual/distraction     
(movies, toys), and environmental modifications (developmental care, cobedding). All met the core criteria of being RCTs
with infants ≤3 years comparing non-pharmacological interventions to no-treatment controls.                             
